          "location": "comparison_tables[5].rows[1].cells[4]",
          "problem": "The cell says the s. 23(b) filing sentence leaves open 'anything about electronic prescriptions'. That is accurate about the statute, but the section never mentions that 247 CMR 9.16(2) requires Schedule II prescriptions to be segregated on paper and electronically separable in electronic form.",
          "rationale": "The section's declared scope is the s. 23(b) separate file for written Schedule II prescriptions, and every statement it makes about that file is correct. A reader could still take 'leaves open' to mean Massachusetts has no rule for electronic Schedule II records. The table is expressly titled as a s. 23 table, so the risk of misleading a candidate is small. A one-clause pointer would close it.",
