          "location": "orientation[11]; orientation[13]",
          "problem": "The section describes 21 CFR 1306.07 as the regulation governing maintenance and detoxification narcotic drugs, and says 'two further paragraphs', (c) and (f), mark its edges. Since 2026-04-01, 1306.07 has also contained paragraphs (g) and (h), which let EMS professionals administer (not prescribe) Schedule II-V drugs under standing or verbal orders.",
          "rationale": "Paragraphs (g) and (h) fall outside the section's declared scope (maintenance and detoxification limits). Every proposition about (a)-(d) and (f) matches the current text, including the (d) text effective 2026-07-09. The statement that no paragraph provides for prescribing a Schedule II narcotic for maintenance or detoxification treatment remains true. This is a structural incompleteness, not a legal error.",
